 <h1>How Brain assembled itself</h1>
 <p>__LESSONS__ lessons across __PROJECTS__ projects, accumulated __FIRSTDATE__ to __LASTDATE__.</p>
 <h2>The co-verification graph</h2>
 <p>An edge forms when two systems are stress-tested together: <span class="c">__EDGES__ edges</span>,
 __SAFE__ of them marked compatible. Connected components give __NGROUPS__ emergent clusters,
 the largest holding __BIG__ systems. Groups are derived on every run, never stored.</p>
 <h2>The frontier</h2>
 <p>__SEAMS__ untested pairs share at least two tags with something already proven.
 Strongest: __SEAMA__ + __SEAMB__ (__SEAMTAGS__ shared tags).</p>
 <h2>What is uncertain</h2>
 <p><span class="r">__INFERRED__ of __EDGES__ edges</span> were mined from prose rather than an
 explicit <span class="mono">Composed:</span> field. __TOPEN__ tensions are open, including ones
 asking whether a single entry should draw an edge at all and whether illustrative mentions are
 being misread as composition.</p>
 <h2>Provenance</h2>
 <p>__VERIFIED__ lessons verified first-hand; <span class="r">__UNVERIFIED__</span> not yet confirmed.</p>
